\f0\fs24 \cf2 <$Scr_Ps::0>
\f1\fs22 Dr Kathy Logan went among the Elvi mourning their dead. She went to the morgue and funeral parlours. She collected blood and lung samples, and sealed them in numbered cryovials which she packed into insulated specimen cases\'97the kind Kathy often used as eskies, complete with \cf0 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
temperature loggers and tamper seals. No one at a party would presume to hit on her when they saw those tax-off boxes.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs24 \cf2 <!$Scr_Ps::0><$Scr_Ps::1>
\f1\fs22 Kathy spoke with mourners and discovered some were 
\fs20 GET BENT
\fs22  survivors; they\'92d all been shoulder-to-shoulder, or embracing or holding hands in the partying crowd when Elvi started stumbling and grabbing them for support. They were pale and sweaty; some shivered, others seemed confused or glassy-eyed. They vomited. They folded at the knees. Some sat down and could not get up again. The crowd closed around them as people tried to help, then opened again as more Elvi went down. Survivors told Kathy of holding friends upright until they could no longer bear their weight, of hands going slack in theirs, of people collapsing unconscious while everyone around them shouted for medics. Then the crush began and nobody could tell who was sick, who had fallen, and who was being trampled. Kathy asked the survivors if they would give her samples of their blood, and Holy Aunt Kathy was never refused. She obtained samples from Elvi who had arrived on Bent Street after the dying began, and from Elvi who had stayed well away from GET BENT and wished everyone else had done the same. \
Hover-copts made twice-daily trips, shuttling Kathy between Sublime Point and the Ghetto\'97even landing on the ground under the Layer to save her time. They were an imposing sight in Shakti Enterprises livery, in colours that resembled the make-up palette only a first-class escort could afford.\
On the first return trip, Kathy transported three cadavers for autopsies in sealed body bags inside rigid isolation shells, as well as her harvest of pathology samples.\
Eloise gave Kathy another lab in the Ruined Castle facility. When Kathy walked in lights blinked alive, and  sequencers, PCR machines, biosafety cabinets, ultracentrifuges, and banks of -80\'b0C freezers sparkled at her. There was not a scratch on chair chrome, a scuff on instrument casing or a smudge on any shiny surface. 
\f2\i This girl wants to own me and mine for seven generations
\f1\i0 , Kathy thought. Eloise would no doubt claim all work product as Shakti IP.\
Within six hours of the lab welcoming her with rookie enthusiasm, sequencing showed high-titre viral material. Early the next day Kathy had garnered enough genome coverage to see a common backbone among the material, with two variants\'97one platform, two different payloads. By the end of the day, she\'92d designed payload-specific PCR assays and, from there, she could start screening for the variants she called 
\f2\i Chilli
\f1\i0  and 
\f2\i Pickle
\f1\i0 . A day later, she was recovering viable virus in cell cultures for Pickle; Chilli took a day longer due to its lower and more variable titre.\
Kathy concluded from lung pathology and presence of Pickle in the airways that it was transmitted through the air. She\'92d parked the dark thought that it was literally an Airborne virus.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl220\sb220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs24 \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 <!$Scr_Ps::1><$Scr_Ps::0>
\f1\fs22 The next day saw a new outbreak of Pickle. Though deaths were not as catastrophic as the first, the recurrence was chilling. That it had broken out it two parts of the city with large populations of Elvi struck Kathy as no coincidence. \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Similar to the first outbreak, one Elvi could die while another\'97sometimes in intimate contact\'97could survive. \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs24 \cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
<!$Scr_Ps::0><$Scr_Ps::1>
\f1\fs22 A hover-copt was already on the Sublime Point pad by the time she\'92d made it up from her Ruined Castle lab. By design, it was not a quick or easy trip; emergencies have never been reckoned into it. Once in the air, Kathy analysed reports of the new outbreak. Elvi were already dead, others were sick and not expected to survive. And there were a few who\'92d shared the same streets, bars and rooms and showed no symptoms at all. By time she\'92d landed, she\'92d plotted locations and severity from the incident reports; even a child could see a target on the map. Kathy had the pilot land her in the middle of it; she spent hours gathering samples, including from among the unaffected, then hightailed her way back to Eloise\'92s compound. \
Kathy stayed in the lab most of the night while she ran tests and conducted autopsies. A pattern quickly developed, but she wanted to process all the samples before she\'92d pronounce a conclusion. There was a comfortable bed in a side room, but she never landed on it. Patches kept her going.\
Both the 
\fs20 GET BENT
\fs22  samples, and samples from the Ghetto samples of the afflicted yielded an abundance of Pickle and an absence of Chilli, while those who were heavily exposed and yet remained well carried varying levels of Chilli. Some Elvi carried a great deal of the Chilli vector; others carried less; some had only traces. Those with Chilli also exhibited small amounts of Pickle in respiratory samples. They had breathed the Pickle and survived.\
Among the wider control samples of both populations, no Pickle was present while Chilli was rare and in varying levels. Chilli was in the population before Pickle had showed up. That fact itched Kathy\'92s curiosity, because both viruses shared a common platform. They\'92d both been engineered, probably in the same lab; the more Kathy looked at them, the more their clean, repeated architecture around payload junctions was visible. They had an identical backbone, identical payload insertion boundaries, and radically different cargo.\
Yet the nastier Pickle had appeared only days ago. Kathy smelled a profit motive.\
She divided matched Elvi cell cultures. Pickle went into one batch by itself. Chilli went into another and was allowed to establish before Kathy gave it a course of Pickle.\
In the first batch, Pickle\'92s payload signal rose as the it reproduced.\
It entered the Chilli cultures too. Kathy could detect it there. What it didn\'92t do was multiply.\
Kathy repeated the test with fresh cultures. In one run, she altered the amount of Pickle. In another, she altered the amount of Chilli. She introduced Pickle to a Chilli culture earlier. In another she introduced it later. In all tests where she introduced Pickle to a Chilli culture, it dwindled. In the no-Chilli cultures, Pickle took over.\
The she introduced Chilli to Pickle cultures. The results were all the same; Pickle died in the presence of Chilli, and then disappeared without trace. \
Kathy needed more blood samples. Elvi turned out in numbers, eager to assist the Great Aunt, and queued by the grounded hover-copt.\
Back in the lab, Kathy screened the fresh samples. In a very small percentage, she found Chilli. Whatever connected the carriers, Kathy could not see it in where they lived or where they worked. What Kathy didn\'92t see at the time: there was a demographic hole in her sample distribution, one that centred around American Sound Studios.
